nodes.hyperparam_def:
- embedding_dim (D): Dimension of the trainable ID embeddings for all users and items in the interaction graph. It controls the capacity of the collaborative representation space; in experiments it is fixed to 64 for all models for fair comparison.
- distilled_feature_dim (D'): Dimension of the modality-specific content space after projecting raw visual, acoustic, and textual features through a linear layer and nonlinearity. It controls how rich the content-side representation is; typically chosen comparable to the ID embedding size and tuned on validation. :contentReference[oaicite:1]{index=1}
- num_gcn_layers (L): Number of stacked graph convolutional layers used to propagate messages over the refined user–item graph. It controls how many hops of neighbors contribute to each embedding; the paper mainly uses L = 2 and shows that deeper stacks may over-smooth representations. :contentReference[oaicite:2]{index=2}
- num_routing_iterations (T): Number of routing iterations in the prototypical network that updates a user’s preference prototype from her interacted items. Larger T lets the prototype move further toward content-consistent neighbors but risks oversmoothing; the ablation varies T (e.g., 1–3) and tunes it per dataset. :contentReference[oaicite:3]{index=3}
- learning_rate: Step size of the Adam optimizer used to train all parameters (embeddings, projection matrices, base vectors). Searched over {0.0001, 0.001, 0.01, 0.1, 1} and selected based on validation Recall@10. :contentReference[oaicite:4]{index=4}
- reg_weight_lambda: L2 regularization coefficient in the BPR loss, applied to model parameters to prevent overfitting on sparse implicit data. Tuned in {0.00001, 0.0001, 0.001, 0.01, 0.1} on the validation set. :contentReference[oaicite:5]{index=5}
- early_stopping_patience: Number of epochs without improvement in validation Recall@10 before training is stopped. Set to 20 consecutive epochs to avoid overfitting while keeping training efficient. :contentReference[oaicite:6]{index=6}

- L: Number of collaborative graph propagation layers. Typical values: {1,2,3,4}
- K: Number of modality graph embedding layers. Typical values: {1,2,3,4}
- H: Number of hypergraph embedding layers. Typical values: {1,2,3,4}
- A: Number of hyperedges. Typical values: {1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256}
- α: Adjustable factor for fusing global embeddings. Typical values: {0.1,0.2,...,1.0}
- ρ: Dropout ratio for hypergraph dependencies. Typical values: {0.1,0.2,...,1.0}
- λ2: Weight for hypergraph contrastive loss. Typical values: {1e-6,1e-5,...,0.1}

- Number of layers (K): depth of stacked graph convolution; typical 2 for citation benchmarks. :contentReference[oaicite:2]{index=2}
- Hidden units (H): width of the hidden GCN layer; typical 16 for Citeseer/Cora/Pubmed, 64 for NELL. :contentReference[oaicite:3]{index=3}
- Dropout rate: dropout applied during training for regularization; typical 0.5 (citation graphs) / 0.1 (NELL). :contentReference[oaicite:4]{index=4}
- L2 regularization (weight decay): applied (notably on the first layer weights); typical 5e-4 (citation graphs) / 1e-5 (NELL). :contentReference[oaicite:5]{index=5}
- Learning rate (lr): Adam step size; typical 0.01. :contentReference[oaicite:6]{index=6}
- Early stopping window: stop if validation loss does not improve for N epochs; typical 10. :contentReference[oaicite:7]{index=7}
- Self-loop trade-off (λ): weight on self-connections in A~ = A + λI; default corresponds to λ=1 (A+I), but can be tuned/learned. :contentReference[oaicite:8]{index=8}
